---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Professional" description="Zachary Drake — unified communications, enterprise collaboration, and the practical engineering behind DrakeLabs.">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">ZACHARY DRAKE / PROFESSIONAL</p><h1>Communications<br />people <em>depend on.</em></h1><p class="lead">My professional focus is unified communications and contact center technology: supporting the platforms, call flows, and connections that keep people working together.</p><div class="chips"><span>Unified communications</span><span>Contact centers</span><span>Enterprise collaboration</span></div></section>
  <section class="section two-col" aria-labelledby="career-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CAREER OVERVIEW</p><h2 id="career-heading">From telecom operations<br />to enterprise collaboration.</h2><p>My career has grown through telecommunications roles in healthcare and enterprise environments, from mobile-device and voice support to unified communications engineering.</p><p>That experience includes roles at Einstein Healthcare Network and USI Insurance Services, work at Cerner supporting Einstein, and a telecommunications contractor role at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP). Across those settings, the work connects technology with the people and business processes relying on it.</p></div><div class="manifesto"><span>THE ENGINEERING APPROACH</span><h3>Understand the service.</h3><p>Follow the problem across platforms, connectivity, call routing, and the user experience.</p><span>PLAN THE CHANGE</span><h3>Make the next step deliberate.</h3><p>Work through dependencies, maintenance planning, validation, and documentation.</p><span>WORK WITH PEOPLE</span><h3>Translate between teams.</h3><p>Coordinate with business stakeholders, vendors, carriers, and fellow engineers.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="experience-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE</p><h2 id="experience-heading">Technology in context.</h2></div></div><div class="cards">
    <article class="card"><span class="number">01 / COLLABORATION</span><h3>Voice &amp; collaboration platforms</h3><p>Cisco Unified Communications Manager, Unity Connection, Webex, and related voice infrastructure. Supporting the services behind everyday business communication.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">02 / CONTACT CENTER</span><h3>Routing &amp; the agent experience</h3><p>Cisco UCCE, CVP, Finesse, and CUIC, with work spanning call flows, routing, reporting, and production troubleshooting.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">03 / OPERATIONS</span><h3>The connections between systems</h3><p>SIP and carrier connectivity, platform lifecycle work, operational documentation, and coordination across technical and business teams.</p></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section" id="selected-work" aria-labelledby="work-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SELECTED WORK</p><h2 id="work-heading">Change with a purpose.</h2></div></div><p class="timeline-intro">Selected examples of platform changes, service integration, and operational work across my career.</p><div class="lined-list career-work">
    <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Collaboration &amp; contact center upgrades</h3><p>Planning, testing, and execution work for Cisco collaboration and contact center platform upgrades, with attention to dependencies and production change windows.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Emergency calling migration</h3><p>Work on moving emergency-calling services from Cisco Emergency Responder to Intrado E911.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Call recording &amp; call-flow documentation</h3><p>Calabrio platform migration work and enterprise contact center routing documentation, connecting platform changes with operational understanding.</p></div></article>
    <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Acquisition integration</h3><p>Supporting the integration of acquired organizations into enterprise voice and collaboration services, working across business teams, vendors, and carriers.</p></div></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section two-col" aria-labelledby="lab-connection-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHERE DRAKELABS FITS</p><h2 id="lab-connection-heading">The same questions.<br />A different scale.</h2><p>At work, communications need to be dependable and usable. At home, my family needs a media experience they can navigate without a support call. Both make me think about the whole service, not just whether a process is running.</p><p>The learning runs both ways. At work, I develop habits around troubleshooting, planning changes, documenting decisions, and thinking about the people who depend on a service. Those habits help me improve what I build and run at home.</p><p>At home, I have room to explore unfamiliar tools, make mistakes, and work through problems at my own pace. What I learn about Ubuntu, the command line, Docker, and automation broadens the perspective I bring back to work. The environments are different, but the curiosity and problem-solving carry across.</p></div><div class="lined-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Design for adoption</h3><p>Standardizing family playback clients and simplifying access made the people using the system part of the design.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}journal/#designing-for-family`}>Read the family-access story →</a></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Learn through operations</h3><p>Linux and Docker became familiar through real maintenance and troubleshooting.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}infrastructure/#learning-linux`}>Explore the lab learning →</a></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Keep a useful record</h3><p>Document decisions, lessons, and how AI contributed so the work can be understood and reviewed.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}journal/#ai-in-the-process`}>How the work was done →</a></div></article></div></section>
  <section class="note-strip"><p class="eyebrow">PROFESSIONAL LINKS</p><h2>A profile that connects the work.</h2><p>Connect with me on LinkedIn for my professional background and experience.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-drake-56454492/">View my LinkedIn profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}projects/`}>Explore the personal projects →</a></section>
</Layout>
